# recording  ticks  slot  requires
#
# slot      which save game in plans/artifacts/P0.5-make-fixture.sh the run boots from.
#           1 = movement fixture, 2 = combat, 3 = beatdown.
# requires  simevents counters that must be NON-ZERO for this recording, or '-' for none.
#           This column exists because P0.5b shipped a recording called 'attack' that never
#           attacked, and three matching digests could not tell anyone. A digest proves the world
#           changed; only these say WHICH code ran.
#
#           'map_event' is on every row as a canary. It is emitted during map load, so a zero
#           there means no map loaded at all -- which is exactly the state every Linux CI run was
#           in until P0.5c, hashing an empty world and passing.
smoke        600   1  map_event,step
patrol       2000  1  map_event,step
melee        2956  2  map_event,attack,hit,die,step,levelup,loot,power
beatdown     2956  3  map_event,attack,hit,step,power,hazard_hit,lowhp_start,lowhp_stop
